--------------------------------------------------------------------
OBSERVATIONS (not failures; for the backlog)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
OBS-1 (test strength, 2(c)): with the contract's prescribed fixture (ONE creep
  finding) the `Count == 1` assertion also passes on master, because master
  renders the sentence once per creep row and there is only one such row. Only
  the position assertion discriminates against master; the count assertion is
  exercised by mutB. A two-creep-finding fixture would make the count assertion
  discriminate on its own. The test as written matches the contract exactly, so
  this is not a defect against acceptance 2.
OBS-2 (test strength, 2(a)): the money assertions are `strings.Contains` over
  the whole `<tr>`, not per-cell in order, and wantMoney[0] repeats
  ">$1,655.30<" (Payment and Annual share the fixture value), so cell ORDER is
  unasserted. The contract only requires the hardcoded formatMoney strings;
  ordered per-cell money parity is checker-second's item 3.
OBS-3 (pre-existing, master-native): 642 elements extend past a 390 px viewport
  inside `overflow-x-auto` regions on /insights — identical count on master and
  branch, page scrollWidth == innerWidth on both. No page-level overflow.
